  "DuuaPBDmdpck": {
    "proposition_id": "DuuaPBDmdpck",
    "text": "To address the problem, we need to consider the relationship between $\\ell_2$ regularization and the bias-variance tradeoff in linear regression",
    "source_node": "YYAX",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "ohE6JuqoQKAu": {
    "proposition_id": "ohE6JuqoQKAu",
    "text": "The bias-variance tradeoff is the tradeoff between the model's ability to fit the training data (low-bias high-variance) and its ability to generalize to new data (high-bias low-variance)",
    "source_node": "YYAX",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "oTPHNXHbG7cK": {
    "proposition_id": "oTPHNXHbG7cK",
    "text": "$\\ell_2$ regularization adds a penalty term to the objective function, which is proportional to the magnitude of the model's weights",
    "source_node": "YYAX",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "rR7ajVy23Xvc": {
    "proposition_id": "rR7ajVy23Xvc",
    "text": "This penalty term encourages the model to have smaller weights, which in turn reduces the variance of the model",
    "source_node": "YYAX",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "tfyJsGT5iLJr": {
    "proposition_id": "tfyJsGT5iLJr",
    "text": "However, by reducing the variance of the model, we also increase its bias, as the model becomes less complex and is unable to capture some of the subtle patterns in the data",
    "source_node": "YYAX",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
    "evidence": [],
    "metadata": {
      "round": 0
    }
  },
  "B3xWQu8QdLzL": {
    "proposition_id": "B3xWQu8QdLzL",
    "text": "Therefore, as you increase the $\\ell_2$ regularization coefficient, the model's bias will increase while its variance will decrease",
    "source_node": "YYAX",
    "source_role": "Knowlegable Expert",
    "confidence": 0.5,
    "status": "belief",
    "scope": "pairwise",
    "dependencies": [],
